      "gitDiff": "diff --git a/.github/workflows/archive-aes-cloud.yml b/.github/workflows/archive-aes-cloud.yml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f4ebd7f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.github/workflows/archive-aes-cloud.yml\n@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@\n+name: Experimental Archive AES and timestamps\n+\n+on:\n+  push:\n+    branches: [main]\n+    paths:\n+      - '.github/workflows/archive-aes-cloud.yml'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/experiments/archive-aes/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/archive/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/lib/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-archive-aes-cloud.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-bsdtar.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-development.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud-bsdtar.mjs'\n+  pull_request:\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+\n+permissions:\n+  contents: read\n+\n+concurrency:\n+  group: archive-aes-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n+  cancel-in-progress: false\n+\n+jobs:\n+  archive-aes-experiment:\n+    runs-on: windows-2022\n+    timeout-minutes: 30\n+    env:\n+      CI: 'true'\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Enable checkout of long research paths\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: git config --global core.longpaths true\n+\n+      - name: Check out baseline and inert experimental sources\n+        id: checkout\n+        uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4\n+        with:\n+          persist-credentials: false\n+          fetch-depth: 1\n+\n+      - name: Select pinned Node runtime\n+        uses: actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020 # v4\n+        with:\n+          node-version: '24.16.0'\n+          architecture: x64\n+          check-latest: false\n+\n+      - name: Select owned evidence directory\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-archive-aes-ci-evidence-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          'REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE=' + $evidence | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_ENV -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+          'ARCHIVE_AES_OBSERVATIONS=' + (Join-Path $evidence 'observations') | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_ENV -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+\n+      - name: Compose authenticated experimental overlay in hosted checkout\n+        id: compose\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-archive-aes-cloud.mjs --phase compose --evidence \"$env:REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Acquire authenticated test-only original 7-Zip\n+        id: bootstrap\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-archive-aes-cloud.mjs --phase bootstrap --evidence \"$env:REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Run thirteen experimental Archive test files with durable evidence\n+        id: verification\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $output = Join-Path $env:REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE 'verification'\n+          $acquisition = Join-Path $env:REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE 'original-acquisition.json'\n+          $composition = Join-Path $env:REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE 'composition.json'\n+          node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud.mjs --scope archive-aes-experiment --output \"$output\" --bootstrap-manifest \"$acquisition\" --overlay-manifest \"$composition\" --timeout-ms 1200000\n+\n+      - name: Acquire explicit paired Microsoft archive oracle for future broader tests\n+        if: always() && steps.bootstrap.outcome == 'success'\n+        id: bsdtar_acquisition\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-bsdtar.mjs --evidence \"$env:REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Verify paired original oracle starts and reports the pinned version\n+        if: always() && steps.bsdtar_acquisition.outcome == 'success'\n+        id: bsdtar_smoke\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud-bsdtar.mjs --evidence \"$env:REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Prepare remaining Automation Sketch and Backup original inputs\n+        if: always() && steps.bsdtar_smoke.outcome == 'success'\n+        id: development_prerequisites\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-development.mjs --evidence \"$env:REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Check composed sources after execution and prerequisite preparation\n+        if: always() && steps.compose.outcome == 'success'\n+        id: postrun\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-archive-aes-cloud.mjs --phase verify-after --evidence \"$env:REA_ARCHIVE_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Package bounded portable experimental evidence\n+        id: evidence\n+        if: always()\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-archive-aes-ci-evidence-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $evidence -Force | Out-Null\n+          @{ schema = 'rea-archive-aes-workflow-attempt/v1'; sourceCommit = $env:GITHUB_SHA; runId = $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID; runAttempt = $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT; runnerEnvironment = $env:RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT; checkoutOutcome = '${{ steps.checkout.outcome }}'; composeOutcome = '${{ steps.compose.outcome }}'; acquisitionOutcome = '${{ steps.bootstrap.outcome }}'; verificationOutcome = '${{ steps.verification.outcome }}'; sourceCheckOutcome = '${{ steps.postrun.outcome }}'; pairedOracleAcquisitionOutcome = '${{ steps.bsdtar_acquisition.outcome }}'; pairedOracleSmokeOutcome = '${{ steps.bsdtar_smoke.outcome }}'; experimentalOverlay = $true; productionInstalled = $false; fullArchiveAcceptance = $false; fullParity = $false } | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $evidence 'workflow-attempt.json') -Encoding utf8\n+          $archive = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-archive-aes-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT + '.zip')\n+          Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem\n+          [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($evidence, $archive, [System.IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal, $false)\n+          $archiveBytes = (Get-Item -LiteralPath $archive).Length\n+          if ($archiveBytes -gt 15 * 1024 * 1024) {\n+            $fallback = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-archive-aes-incomplete-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+            New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $fallback | Out-Null\n+            foreach ($relative in @('workflow-attempt.json', 'composition.json', 'original-acquisition.json', 'postrun-source-check.json', 'verification/attempt-validation.json', 'bsdtar-original-acquisition.json', 'bsdtar-original-smoke.json')) {\n+              $candidate = Join-Path $evidence $relative\n+              if ((Test-Path -LiteralPath $candidate -PathType Leaf) -and (Get-Item -LiteralPath $candidate).Length -le 1024 * 1024) {\n+                Copy-Item -LiteralPath $candidate -Destination (Join-Path $fallback $relative.Replace('/', '-'))\n+              }\n+            }\n+            @{ schema = 'rea-cloud-evidence-storage-failure/v1'; status = 'failed'; fullArchiveBytes = $archiveBytes; limitBytes = 15 * 1024 * 1024; fullEvidenceUploaded = $false; sourceSnapshotsUploaded = $false; rawLogsUploaded = $false; reason = 'The complete experimental evidence exceeded the bounded artifact budget. This diagnostic fallback is incomplete.' } | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $fallback 'storage-failure.json') -Encoding utf8\n+            $archive = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-archive-aes-incomplete-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT + '.zip')\n+            [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($fallback, $archive, [System.IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal, $false)\n+            'artifact_path=' + $archive | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+            throw 'Full experimental evidence exceeded 15 MiB. Only incomplete diagnostic records will be uploaded.'\n+          }\n+          'artifact_path=' + $archive | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+\n+      - name: Preserve experimental success or failure evidence\n+        if: always() && steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path != ''\n+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n+        with:\n+          name: archive-aes-experimental-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}\n+          path: ${{ steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path }}\n+          if-no-files-found: error\n+          compression-level: 0\n+          retention-days: 1\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/browser-flow-vault-cloud.yml b/.github/workflows/browser-flow-vault-cloud.yml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..6333e12\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.github/workflows/browser-flow-vault-cloud.yml\n@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@\n+name: Cloud Flow and Vault browser acceptance\n+\n+on:\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+  push:\n+    branches: [main]\n+    paths:\n+      - '.github/workflows/browser-flow-vault-cloud.yml'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/browser-tests/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud-browser.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/flow/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/vault/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/lib/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/public/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/server.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/catalog.mjs'\n+  pull_request:\n+    paths:\n+      - '.github/workflows/browser-flow-vault-cloud.yml'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/browser-tests/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud-browser.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/flow/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/vault/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/lib/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/public/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/server.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/catalog.mjs'\n+\n+permissions:\n+  contents: read\n+concurrency:\n+  group: flow-vault-browser-${{ github.ref }}\n+  cancel-in-progress: false\n+\n+jobs:\n+  finite-real-chromium:\n+    runs-on: windows-2022\n+    timeout-minutes: 20\n+    env:\n+      CI: 'true'\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Enable long source paths\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: git config --global core.longpaths true\n+      - name: Check out the exact source revision\n+        id: checkout\n+        uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4\n+        with:\n+          persist-credentials: false\n+          fetch-depth: 1\n+      - name: Select pinned Node runtime\n+        uses: actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020 # v4\n+        with:\n+          node-version: '24.16.0'\n+          architecture: x64\n+          check-latest: false\n+      - name: Select owned evidence outside the source tree\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-browser-evidence-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          'REA_BROWSER_EVIDENCE='+$evidence | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_ENV -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+          $browserCache=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-playwright-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          'PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH='+$browserCache | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_ENV -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+      - name: Install exact locked browser tooling and matching Chromium on the hosted runner\n+        id: acquire\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud-browser.mjs --phase acquire --evidence \"$env:REA_BROWSER_EVIDENCE\"\n+      - name: Run twelve finite current Flow and Vault real-browser scenarios\n+        id: browser\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud-browser.mjs --phase verify --evidence \"$env:REA_BROWSER_EVIDENCE\"\n+      - name: Package bounded portable browser evidence after every observable attempt\n+        id: evidence\n+        if: always()\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-browser-evidence-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $evidence -Force | Out-Null\n+          @{schema='rea-cloud-browser-workflow-attempt/v1';sourceCommit=$env:GITHUB_SHA;runId=$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID;runAttempt=$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT;runnerEnvironment=$env:RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT;checkoutOutcome='${{ steps.checkout.outcome }}';acquisitionOutcome='${{ steps.acquire.outcome }}';browserOutcome='${{ steps.browser.outcome }}';statusBeforePackaging='${{ job.status }}';historicalReceiptsRebound=$false;originalProductComparisons=0;acceptancePreclaimed=$false}|ConvertTo-Json|Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $evidence 'browser-workflow-attempt.json') -Encoding utf8\n+          $archive=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-browser-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT+'.zip')\n+          Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem\n+          [IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($evidence,$archive,[IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal,$false)\n+          $limit=15*1024*1024;$bytes=(Get-Item -LiteralPath $archive).Length\n+          if($bytes -gt $limit){\n+            $fallback=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-browser-incomplete-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+            New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $fallback | Out-Null\n+            $retained=@();$omitted=@()\n+            foreach($file in Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $evidence -File){\n+              if($file.Length -le 1024*1024){Copy-Item -LiteralPath $file.FullName -Destination (Join-Path $fallback $file.Name);$retained+=$file.Name}\n+              elseif($file.Extension -eq '.txt'){$target=Join-Path $fallback ($file.BaseName+'.tail.txt');$logInput=[IO.File]::OpenRead($file.FullName);$logOutput=[IO.File]::Create($target);try{$logInput.Position=[Math]::Max(0,$logInput.Length-256*1024);$logInput.CopyTo($logOutput)}finally{$logOutput.Dispose();$logInput.Dispose()};$omitted+=@{file=$file.Name;originalBytes=$file.Length;tailOnly=$true}}\n+              else{$omitted+=@{file=$file.Name;bytes=$file.Length;tailOnly=$false}}\n+            }\n+            @{schema='rea-cloud-evidence-storage-failure/v1';status='failed';fullArchiveBytes=$bytes;limitBytes=$limit;completeEvidenceUploaded=$false;screenshotsAndTracesUploaded=$false;sourceSnapshotsUploaded=$false;retainedFiles=$retained;omittedOrTailed=$omitted;reason='Full browser evidence exceeded15MiB; this diagnostic fallback cannot establish complete portable acceptance evidence.'}|ConvertTo-Json -Depth 6|Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $fallback 'storage-failure.json') -Encoding utf8\n+            $archive=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-browser-incomplete-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT+'.zip')\n+            [IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($fallback,$archive,[IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal,$false)\n+            if((Get-Item -LiteralPath $archive).Length -le $limit){'artifact_path='+$archive|Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append}\n+            throw 'Full browser evidence exceeded15MiB; only an explicitly incomplete bounded fallback can be uploaded.'\n+          }\n+          'artifact_path='+$archive|Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+      - name: Preserve the portable browser evidence\n+        if: always() && steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path != ''\n+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n+        with:\n+          name: flow-vault-browser-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}\n+          path: ${{ steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path }}\n+          if-no-files-found: error\n+          compression-level: 0\n+          retention-days: 1\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/development-cloud.yml b/.github/workflows/development-cloud.yml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..568a19a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.github/workflows/development-cloud.yml\n@@ -0,0 +1,251 @@\n+name: Cloud development oracle experiment\n+\n+on:\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+  push:\n+    branches: [main]\n+    paths:\n+      - '.github/workflows/development-cloud.yml'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/lib/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/public/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/tests/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/experiments/bsdtar-oracle/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/server.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/catalog.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/package.json'\n+      - 'projects/07-keepass/**'\n+      - 'projects/08-7zip/**'\n+      - 'projects/09-restic/**'\n+      - 'scripts/acquire-windows-release.mjs'\n+  pull_request:\n+    paths:\n+      - '.github/workflows/development-cloud.yml'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/lib/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/public/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/tests/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/experiments/bsdtar-oracle/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/server.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/catalog.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/package.json'\n+      - 'projects/07-keepass/**'\n+      - 'projects/08-7zip/**'\n+      - 'projects/09-restic/**'\n+      - 'scripts/acquire-windows-release.mjs'\n+\n+permissions:\n+  contents: read\n+\n+concurrency:\n+  group: development-oracle-${{ github.ref }}\n+  cancel-in-progress: false\n+\n+jobs:\n+  full-oracle-experiment:\n+    runs-on: windows-2022\n+    timeout-minutes: 50\n+    env:\n+      CI: 'true'\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Enable long research snapshot paths\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: git config --global core.longpaths true\n+\n+      - name: Check out the exact source revision\n+        id: checkout\n+        uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4\n+        with:\n+          persist-credentials: false\n+          fetch-depth: 1\n+\n+      - name: Select the pinned Node runtime\n+        uses: actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020 # v4\n+        with:\n+          node-version: '24.16.0'\n+          architecture: x64\n+          check-latest: false\n+\n+      - name: Select a unique evidence directory\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-development-ci-evidence-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          'REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE=' + $evidence | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_ENV -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+\n+      - name: Compose only the three reviewed oracle-test sources\n+        id: compose\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-bsdtar-oracle-cloud.mjs --phase compose --evidence \"$env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Acquire pinned Flow and Vault prerequisites\n+        id: flow_vault\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-flow-vault.mjs --evidence \"$env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Acquire full and Extra 7-Zip inputs with one bounded bootstrap extraction\n+        id: archive\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $archiveSource = @'\n+          import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n+          import * as fs from 'node:fs/promises';\n+          import path from 'node:path';\n+          import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n+          import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\n+          import { prepareOriginalArchiveOracle } from './products/rea-studio/apps/archive/bootstrap-original.mjs';\n+          assert.equal(process.platform, 'win32'); assert.equal(process.version, 'v24.16.0');\n+          assert.equal(process.env.CI, 'true'); assert.equal(process.env.GITHUB_ACTIONS, 'true'); assert.equal(process.env.RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT, 'github-hosted');\n+          const repository = process.cwd(), evidence = await fs.realpath(process.env.REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE);\n+          const relative = path.relative(await fs.realpath(process.env.RUNNER_TEMP), evidence);\n+          assert(relative && relative !== '..' && !relative.startsWith('..' + path.sep) && !path.isAbsolute(relative));\n+          const sha = bytes => createHash('sha256').update(bytes).digest('hex');\n+          const receiptPath = path.join(evidence, 'archive-original-prerequisites.json');\n+          const record = { schema: 'rea-cloud-archive-original-prerequisites/v1', status: 'running', startedAtUtc: new Date().toISOString(),\n+            execution: Object.fromEntries(['GITHUB_SHA','GITHUB_RUN_ID','GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT','GITHUB_REPOSITORY'].map(name => [name, process.env[name]])),\n+            scope: 'Authenticated full and Extra 7-Zip inputs, with one original 7zr bootstrap extraction of the pinned standalone oracle. Later comparison calls belong to the tests.', assets: [], bootstrapExtractionProcessAttempts: 0, bootstrapExtractionProcesses: 0, originalProcesses: 0, comparisonProcesses: 0, vendorBinariesPublished: false };\n+          async function save(initial = false) {\n+            const temporary = initial ? receiptPath : receiptPath + '.tmp', file = await fs.open(temporary, 'wx');\n+            try { await file.writeFile(JSON.stringify(record, null, 2) + '\\n'); await file.sync(); } finally { await file.close(); }\n+            if (!initial) await fs.rename(temporary, receiptPath);\n+          }\n+          async function authenticate(filename, expected) {\n+            const item = await fs.lstat(filename); assert(item.isFile() && !item.isSymbolicLink()); assert.equal(item.size, expected.bytes);\n+            const bytes = await fs.readFile(filename); assert.equal(sha(bytes), expected.sha256); return bytes;\n+          }\n+          await save(true);\n+          try {\n+            const full = await prepareOriginalArchiveOracle(); assert.equal(full.schema, 'rea-archive-original-acquisition/v1'); assert.equal(full.assets.length, 2);\n+            const pins = { '.local/archive-original/7z2604-x64.exe': { bytes:1664082,sha256:'d54bf805f9f3704d1e8db2fa3498ae7ef2df0312b40b558e7c71c734430a665d' }, '.local/archive-original/7zr.exe': { bytes:602624,sha256:'256feca8e274e5da655e2a284fabafd9f554365eb164862089dacd4e8276d282' } };\n+            for (const asset of full.assets) { assert(pins[asset.path]); await authenticate(path.join(repository, asset.path), pins[asset.path]); record.assets.push({ ...asset, authenticated:true }); }\n+            const provenanceBytes = await fs.readFile('projects/08-7zip/acquisition.json'), provenance = JSON.parse(provenanceBytes);\n+            record.extraSourceManifest = { path:'projects/08-7zip/acquisition.json', bytes:provenanceBytes.length, sha256:sha(provenanceBytes) };\n+            const extra = provenance.artifacts.find(row => row.relative_path === 'artifacts/7z2604-extra.7z');\n+            assert.equal(extra.bytes,1764616); assert.equal(extra.sha256,'dc4b11d3399db18b063630137145f5585d8f7ac847bf3639bd1185d7d1f7cee0');\n+            assert.equal(extra.source_url,'https://github.com/ip7z/7zip/releases/download/26.04/7z2604-extra.7z');\n+            const artifacts = path.join(repository,'projects/08-7zip/artifacts'); await fs.mkdir(artifacts,{recursive:true}); assert(!(await fs.lstat(artifacts)).isSymbolicLink());\n+            const destination = path.join(artifacts,'7z2604-extra.7z');\n+            try { await fs.lstat(destination); }\n+            catch (error) {\n+              if(error.code !== 'ENOENT') throw error;\n+              const response = await fetch(extra.source_url,{signal:AbortSignal.timeout(45000)}); assert(response.ok);\n+              const chunks=[];let total=0;for await(const chunk of response.body){total+=chunk.length;assert(total<=extra.bytes);chunks.push(chunk);}\n+              const bytes=Buffer.concat(chunks);assert.equal(bytes.length,extra.bytes);assert.equal(sha(bytes),extra.sha256);await fs.writeFile(destination,bytes,{flag:'wx'});\n+            }\n+            await authenticate(destination,extra); record.assets.push({path:'projects/08-7zip/artifacts/7z2604-extra.7z',bytes:extra.bytes,sha256:extra.sha256,source_url:extra.source_url,authenticated:true});\n+            const bootstrapPin=pins['.local/archive-original/7zr.exe'],bootstrapBytes=await authenticate(path.join(repository,'.local/archive-original/7zr.exe'),bootstrapPin),extraBootstrap=path.join(artifacts,'7zr.exe');\n+            try { await fs.writeFile(extraBootstrap,bootstrapBytes,{flag:'wx'}); } catch(error){if(error.code!=='EEXIST')throw error;}\n+            await authenticate(extraBootstrap,bootstrapPin);record.assets.push({path:'projects/08-7zip/artifacts/7zr.exe',...bootstrapPin,authenticated:true,source:'authenticated full-oracle bootstrap copy'});\n+            const standalonePin={bytes:1335808,sha256:'15d4c788c148e3677e2fc1c4a01f191fb6669eba4f6acf8a465f0f1a6f1e1260'};\n+            record.bootstrapExtractionProcessAttempts=1;await save();\n+            const extraction=spawnSync(extraBootstrap,['e','-so',destination,'x64/7za.exe'],{cwd:artifacts,shell:false,windowsHide:true,timeout:20000,maxBuffer:2*1024*1024,encoding:'buffer'});\n+            record.bootstrapExtractionProcesses=Number.isInteger(extraction.pid)&&extraction.pid>0?1:0;record.originalProcesses=record.bootstrapExtractionProcesses;\n+            const extracted=extraction.stdout??Buffer.alloc(0),extractionStderr=extraction.stderr??Buffer.alloc(0);\n+            record.bootstrapExtraction={arguments:['e','-so','projects/08-7zip/artifacts/7z2604-extra.7z','x64/7za.exe'],exitCode:extraction.status,signal:extraction.signal,errorCode:extraction.error?.code??null,stdout:{bytes:extracted.length,sha256:sha(extracted)},stderr:{bytes:extractionStderr.length,sha256:sha(extractionStderr)},binaryOutputRetainedInEvidence:false};await save();\n+            assert.equal(extraction.error,undefined);assert.equal(extraction.status,0);assert.equal(record.bootstrapExtractionProcesses,1);assert.equal(extracted.length,standalonePin.bytes);assert.equal(sha(extracted),standalonePin.sha256);\n+            const extraDirectory=path.join(artifacts,'extra'),standaloneDirectory=path.join(extraDirectory,'x64');\n+            for(const directory of [extraDirectory,standaloneDirectory]){try{await fs.mkdir(directory);}catch(error){if(error.code!=='EEXIST')throw error;}const item=await fs.lstat(directory);assert(item.isDirectory()&&!item.isSymbolicLink());}\n+            const standalone=path.join(standaloneDirectory,'7za.exe');try{await fs.writeFile(standalone,extracted,{flag:'wx'});}catch(error){if(error.code!=='EEXIST')throw error;}\n+            await authenticate(standalone,standalonePin);record.assets.push({path:'projects/08-7zip/artifacts/extra/x64/7za.exe',...standalonePin,authenticated:true,source:'single bounded 7zr extraction from the authenticated Extra archive'});\n+            record.status='acquired';record.completedAtUtc=new Date().toISOString();await save();console.log(JSON.stringify({status:record.status,assets:record.assets.length,bootstrapExtractionProcesses:record.bootstrapExtractionProcesses,originalProcesses:record.originalProcesses,comparisonProcesses:0}));\n+          } catch(error){record.status='failed';record.completedAtUtc=new Date().toISOString();record.failure={name:error.name,message:error.message};await save();throw error;}\n+          '@\n+          $archiveSource | & node --input-type=module\n+          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }\n+\n+      - name: Acquire the explicitly paired Microsoft bsdtar images\n+        id: bsdtar\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-bsdtar.mjs --evidence \"$env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Record the separate original bsdtar smoke invocation\n+        id: bsdtar_smoke\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud-bsdtar.mjs --evidence \"$env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Acquire additional Automation, Sketch and Backup prerequisites\n+        id: additional\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-development.mjs --evidence \"$env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Bind the same-attempt prerequisite receipts\n+        id: prerequisite_manifest\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $definitions = @(\n+            @('flow-vault','prerequisite-acquisition.json','rea-cloud-flow-vault-prerequisites/v1','acquired'),\n+            @('archive','archive-original-prerequisites.json','rea-cloud-archive-original-prerequisites/v1','acquired'),\n+            @('bsdtar','bsdtar-original-acquisition.json','rea-cloud-bsdtar-original-prerequisites/v1','acquired'),\n+            @('additional','development-prerequisites.json','rea-cloud-development-additional-prerequisites/v1','acquired'),\n+            @('bsdtar-smoke','bsdtar-original-smoke.json','rea-cloud-bsdtar-original-smoke/v1','passed')\n+          )\n+          $receipts = @()\n+          foreach ($definition in $definitions) {\n+            $receiptPath = Join-Path $env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE $definition[1]\n+            $value = Get-Content -LiteralPath $receiptPath -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json\n+            if ($value.schema -ne $definition[2] -or $value.status -ne $definition[3]) { throw ('Incomplete prerequisite: ' + $definition[0]) }\n+            $receipts += @{ role=$definition[0]; file=$definition[1]; bytes=(Get-Item -LiteralPath $receiptPath).Length; sha256=(Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $receiptPath -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant(); schema=$value.schema; status=$value.status }\n+          }\n+          @{ schema='rea-cloud-full-oracle-prerequisites/v1'; status='acquired'; execution=@{ GITHUB_SHA=$env:GITHUB_SHA; GITHUB_RUN_ID=$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID; GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT=$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT; GITHUB_REPOSITORY=$env:GITHUB_REPOSITORY }; receipts=$receipts; productTestsExecutedByManifest=0 } | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 8 | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE 'full-oracle-prerequisites.json') -Encoding utf8\n+\n+      - name: Run every current test in the explicit oracle-test epoch\n+        id: full_suite\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $manifest = Join-Path $env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE 'full-oracle-prerequisites.json'\n+          $composition = Join-Path $env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE 'bsdtar-composition.json'\n+          node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud.mjs --scope full-oracle-experiment --output \"$env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE\" --bootstrap-manifest \"$manifest\" --overlay-manifest \"$composition\" --timeout-ms 2400000\n+\n+      - name: Recheck the oracle source composition after every observable attempt\n+        id: oracle_postcheck\n+        if: always() && steps.compose.outcome != 'skipped' && steps.compose.outcome != ''\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-bsdtar-oracle-cloud.mjs --phase verify-after --evidence \"$env:REA_DEVELOPMENT_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Package bounded portable evidence even on failure\n+        id: evidence\n+        if: always()\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-development-ci-evidence-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $evidence -Force | Out-Null\n+          @{ schema='rea-cloud-full-oracle-workflow-attempt/v1'; sourceCommit=$env:GITHUB_SHA; runId=$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID; runAttempt=$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT; runnerEnvironment=$env:RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT; checkoutOutcome='${{ steps.checkout.outcome }}'; compositionOutcome='${{ steps.compose.outcome }}'; flowVaultOutcome='${{ steps.flow_vault.outcome }}'; archiveOutcome='${{ steps.archive.outcome }}'; bsdtarOutcome='${{ steps.bsdtar.outcome }}'; bsdtarSmokeOutcome='${{ steps.bsdtar_smoke.outcome }}'; additionalOutcome='${{ steps.additional.outcome }}'; testOutcome='${{ steps.full_suite.outcome }}'; oraclePostcheckOutcome='${{ steps.oracle_postcheck.outcome }}'; statusBeforePackaging='${{ job.status }}'; historicalDevelopmentReceiptOverwritten=$false; productAcceptancePreclaimed=$false } | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $evidence 'workflow-attempt.json') -Encoding utf8\n+          $archive = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-development-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT + '.zip')\n+          Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem\n+          [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($evidence,$archive,[System.IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal,$false)\n+          $archiveBytes = (Get-Item -LiteralPath $archive).Length\n+          $limit = 15 * 1024 * 1024\n+          if ($archiveBytes -gt $limit) {\n+            $fallback = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-development-incomplete-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+            New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $fallback | Out-Null\n+            $retained=@();$omitted=@();$tailed=@()\n+            foreach ($name in @('workflow-attempt.json','attempt-validation.json','events.jsonl','stdout.txt','stderr.txt','source-before.json','source-after.json','git-baseline-active-source.json','bsdtar-composition.json','bsdtar-postrun-source-check.json','prerequisite-acquisition.json','archive-original-prerequisites.json','bsdtar-original-acquisition.json','bsdtar-original-smoke.json','bsdtar-smoke-stdout.txt','bsdtar-smoke-stderr.txt','development-prerequisites.json','development-prerequisites.events.jsonl','full-oracle-prerequisites.json')) {\n+              $candidate=Join-Path $evidence $name\n+              if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $candidate -PathType Leaf) {\n+                $bytes=(Get-Item -LiteralPath $candidate).Length\n+                if($bytes -le 512*1024){Copy-Item -LiteralPath $candidate -Destination (Join-Path $fallback $name);$retained+=$name}\n+                elseif($name -in @('stdout.txt','stderr.txt')){\n+                  $tailName=$name.Replace('.txt','.tail.txt');$logInput=[IO.File]::OpenRead($candidate);$logTail=[IO.File]::Create((Join-Path $fallback $tailName))\n+                  try{$logInput.Position=[Math]::Max(0,$logInput.Length-256*1024);$logInput.CopyTo($logTail)}finally{$logTail.Dispose();$logInput.Dispose()}\n+                  $retained+=$tailName;$tailed+=@{original=$name;originalBytes=$bytes;retainedTailBytes=256*1024}\n+                }else{$omitted+=@{name=$name;bytes=$bytes}}\n+              }\n+            }\n+            @{schema='rea-cloud-evidence-storage-failure/v1';status='failed';fullArchiveBytes=$archiveBytes;limitBytes=$limit;fullEvidenceUploaded=$false;sourceSnapshotsUploaded=$false;retainedFiles=$retained;truncatedLogs=$tailed;omittedLargeTopLevelFiles=$omitted;reason='Full portable evidence exceeded15MiB. This fallback is incomplete; complete source/raw evidence backup is not established. Streaming test logs may remain in the Actions console.'}|ConvertTo-Json -Depth 8|Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $fallback 'storage-failure.json') -Encoding utf8\n+            $archive=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-development-incomplete-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT + '.zip')\n+            [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($fallback,$archive,[System.IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal,$false)\n+            'artifact_path='+$archive|Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+            throw 'Full evidence exceeded15MiB; only the explicitly incomplete diagnostic fallback will be uploaded.'\n+          }\n+          'artifact_path='+$archive|Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+\n+      - name: Preserve the portable evidence archive\n+        if: always() && steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path != ''\n+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n+        with:\n+          name: development-oracle-windows-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}\n+          path: ${{ steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path }}\n+          if-no-files-found: error\n+          compression-level: 0\n+          retention-days: 1\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/flow-vault-cloud.yml b/.github/workflows/flow-vault-cloud.yml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..a186b95\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.github/workflows/flow-vault-cloud.yml\n@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@\n+name: Cloud Flow and Vault verification\n+\n+on:\n+  push:\n+    branches: [main]\n+    paths:\n+      - '.github/workflows/flow-vault-cloud.yml'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/flow/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/vault/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/lib/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/public/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/server.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/catalog.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/package.json'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-flow-vault.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud-controls.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-preserved-cloud-flow-vault.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-20261015/**'\n+  pull_request:\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+\n+permissions:\n+  contents: read\n+\n+concurrency:\n+  group: flow-vault-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n+  cancel-in-progress: false\n+\n+jobs:\n+  flow-vault:\n+    runs-on: windows-2022\n+    timeout-minutes: 30\n+    env:\n+      CI: 'true'\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Enable exact-byte checkout of long research snapshot paths\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: git config --global core.longpaths true\n+\n+      - name: Check out the exact source revision\n+        id: checkout\n+        uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4\n+        with:\n+          persist-credentials: false\n+          fetch-depth: 1\n+\n+      - name: Select the pinned Node runtime\n+        uses: actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020 # v4\n+        with:\n+          node-version: '24.16.0'\n+          architecture: x64\n+          check-latest: false\n+\n+      - name: Select a unique evidence directory outside the source census\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-flow-vault-ci-evidence-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          'REA_CI_EVIDENCE=' + $evidence | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_ENV -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+\n+      - name: Acquire authenticated test-only original prerequisites\n+        id: prerequisites\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-flow-vault.mjs --evidence \"$env:REA_CI_EVIDENCE\"\n+\n+      - name: Authenticate preserved finite evidence and reject synthetic corruption\n+        id: preservation_integrity\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $report = & node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-preserved-cloud-flow-vault.mjs --self-test\n+          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Preserved finite evidence verification failed.' }\n+          $report | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $env:REA_CI_EVIDENCE 'preserved-flow-vault-integrity.json') -Encoding utf8\n+          $report\n+\n+      - name: Verify collector failure closure with isolated synthetic controls\n+        id: collector_controls\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $controls = Join-Path $env:REA_CI_EVIDENCE 'collector-controls'\n+          node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud-controls.mjs --output \"$controls\"\n+\n+      - name: Run the finite current Flow and Vault suite\n+        id: finite_verification\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $manifest = Join-Path $env:REA_CI_EVIDENCE 'prerequisite-acquisition.json'\n+          node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud.mjs --scope flow-vault --output \"$env:REA_CI_EVIDENCE\" --bootstrap-manifest \"$manifest\" --timeout-ms 1200000\n+\n+      - name: Package portable evidence within the storage limit\n+        id: evidence\n+        if: always()\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-flow-vault-ci-evidence-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $evidence -Force | Out-Null\n+          @{ schema = 'rea-cloud-workflow-attempt/v1'; sourceCommit = $env:GITHUB_SHA; runId = $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID; runAttempt = $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT; runnerEnvironment = $env:RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT; checkoutOutcome = '${{ steps.checkout.outcome }}'; prerequisiteOutcome = '${{ steps.prerequisites.outcome }}'; collectorControlsOutcome = '${{ steps.collector_controls.outcome }}'; finiteVerificationOutcome = '${{ steps.finite_verification.outcome }}'; statusBeforePackaging = '${{ job.status }}'; productTestsClaimed = $false } | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $evidence 'workflow-attempt.json') -Encoding utf8\n+          $archive = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-flow-vault-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT + '.zip')\n+          Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem\n+          [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($evidence, $archive, [System.IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal, $false)\n+          $archiveBytes = (Get-Item -LiteralPath $archive).Length\n+          $limit = 15 * 1024 * 1024\n+          if ($archiveBytes -gt $limit) {\n+            $fallback = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-flow-vault-storage-failure-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+            New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $fallback | Out-Null\n+            $retained = @()\n+            $omitted = @()\n+            $tailed = @()\n+            foreach ($name in @('attempt-validation.json', 'events.jsonl', 'stdout.txt', 'stderr.txt', 'source-before.json', 'source-after.json', 'prerequisite-acquisition.json', 'windows-tar-readiness.json', 'workflow-attempt.json')) {\n+              $candidate = Join-Path $evidence $name\n+              if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $candidate -PathType Leaf) {\n+                $bytes = (Get-Item -LiteralPath $candidate).Length\n+                if ($bytes -le 1024 * 1024) { Copy-Item -LiteralPath $candidate -Destination (Join-Path $fallback $name); $retained += $name }\n+                elseif ($name -in @('stdout.txt', 'stderr.txt')) {\n+                  $tailName = $name.Replace('.txt', '.tail.txt')\n+                  $logInput = [System.IO.File]::OpenRead($candidate)\n+                  $logTail = [System.IO.File]::Create((Join-Path $fallback $tailName))\n+                  try { $logInput.Position = [Math]::Max(0, $logInput.Length - 256 * 1024); $logInput.CopyTo($logTail) }\n+                  finally { $logTail.Dispose(); $logInput.Dispose() }\n+                  $retained += $tailName\n+                  $tailed += @{ original = $name; originalBytes = $bytes; retainedTailBytes = 256 * 1024 }\n+                }\n+                else { $omitted += @{ name = $name; bytes = $bytes } }\n+              }\n+            }\n+            $controlsSummary = Join-Path $evidence 'collector-controls/controls-validation.json'\n+            if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $controlsSummary -PathType Leaf) {\n+              $controlsBytes = (Get-Item -LiteralPath $controlsSummary).Length\n+              if ($controlsBytes -le 1024 * 1024) {\n+                Copy-Item -LiteralPath $controlsSummary -Destination (Join-Path $fallback 'collector-controls-validation.json')\n+                $retained += 'collector-controls-validation.json'\n+              } else { $omitted += @{ name = 'collector-controls/controls-validation.json'; bytes = $controlsBytes } }\n+            }\n+            @{ schema = 'rea-cloud-evidence-storage-failure/v1'; status = 'failed'; fullArchiveBytes = $archiveBytes; limitBytes = $limit; fullEvidenceUploaded = $false; sourceSnapshotsUploaded = $false; retainedFiles = $retained; truncatedLogs = $tailed; omittedLargeTopLevelFiles = $omitted; reason = 'Full portable evidence exceeded the explicitly bounded artifact budget. The fallback is incomplete; do not claim complete evidence backup. Complete streaming test logs may remain available in the Actions console.' } | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 8 | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $fallback 'storage-failure.json') -Encoding utf8\n+            $archive = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-flow-vault-incomplete-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT + '.zip')\n+            [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($fallback, $archive, [System.IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal, $false)\n+            'artifact_path=' + $archive | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+            throw 'Portable evidence exceeded 15 MiB; only the explicitly incomplete diagnostic fallback will be uploaded.'\n+          }\n+          'artifact_path=' + $archive | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+\n+      - name: Preserve evidence even when acquisition or tests fail\n+        if: always() && steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path != ''\n+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n+        with:\n+          name: flow-vault-windows-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}\n+          path: ${{ steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path }}\n+          if-no-files-found: error\n+          compression-level: 0\n+          retention-days: 1\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/publication-integrity-cloud.yml b/.github/workflows/publication-integrity-cloud.yml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..a24be1e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.github/workflows/publication-integrity-cloud.yml\n@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@\n+name: Hosted publication integrity\n+\n+on:\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+  pull_request:\n+    paths:\n+      - '.github/workflows/publication-integrity-cloud.yml'\n+      - 'scripts/verify-cloud-publication.mjs'\n+      - 'scripts/publication-integrity-controls.mjs'\n+      - 'scripts/verify-records.mjs'\n+      - 'scripts/editor-vault-proof-migration.mjs'\n+      - 'scripts/verify-cloud-recovery-records.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/results/cloud-publication-source-transition-20261015/**'\n+\n+permissions:\n+  contents: read\n+\n+concurrency:\n+  group: publication-integrity-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n+  cancel-in-progress: false\n+\n+jobs:\n+  publication-integrity:\n+    runs-on: windows-2022\n+    timeout-minutes: 55\n+    env:\n+      CI: 'true'\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Enable long research paths\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: git config --global core.longpaths true\n+\n+      - name: Check out the exact requested revision\n+        id: checkout\n+        uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4\n+        with:\n+          ref: ${{ github.sha }}\n+          persist-credentials: false\n+          fetch-depth: 1\n+\n+      - name: Select pinned Node runtime\n+        uses: actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020 # v4\n+        with:\n+          node-version: '24.16.0'\n+          architecture: x64\n+          check-latest: false\n+\n+      - name: Regenerate and verify publication metadata with controls\n+        id: verification\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-publication-evidence-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          node scripts/verify-cloud-publication.mjs --evidence \"$evidence\"\n+\n+      - name: Package bounded publication evidence\n+        id: evidence\n+        if: always()\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-publication-evidence-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $evidence -Force | Out-Null\n+          @{ schema = 'rea-hosted-publication-workflow-attempt/v1'; sourceCommit = $env:GITHUB_SHA; runId = $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID; runAttempt = $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT; runnerEnvironment = $env:RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT; checkoutOutcome = '${{ steps.checkout.outcome }}'; verificationOutcome = '${{ steps.verification.outcome }}'; published = $false; historicalReceiptsRewritten = $false; fullDevelopmentSuiteAcceptance = $false; fullParity = $false } | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $evidence 'workflow-attempt.json') -Encoding utf8\n+          $files = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $evidence -File -Recurse)\n+          $rawBytes = ($files | Measure-Object Length -Sum).Sum\n+          $bounded = $files.Count -le 40 -and $rawBytes -le 35 * 1024 * 1024 -and @($files | Where-Object { $_.Length -gt 12 * 1024 * 1024 }).Count -eq 0\n+          $archive = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-publication-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT + '.zip')\n+          Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem\n+          if ($bounded) { [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($evidence, $archive, [System.IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal, $false) }\n+          $complete = $bounded -and (Get-Item -LiteralPath $archive).Length -le 15 * 1024 * 1024\n+          if (-not $complete) {\n+            $fallback = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-publication-incomplete-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+            New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $fallback | Out-Null\n+            foreach ($relative in @('workflow-attempt.json', 'attempt-validation.json', 'controls.json', 'events.jsonl', 'publication-write.stderr.txt', 'publication-recheck.stderr.txt')) {\n+              $candidate = Join-Path $evidence $relative\n+              if ((Test-Path -LiteralPath $candidate -PathType Leaf) -and (Get-Item -LiteralPath $candidate).Length -le 2 * 1024 * 1024) { Copy-Item -LiteralPath $candidate -Destination (Join-Path $fallback $relative) }\n+            }\n+            @{ schema = 'rea-cloud-evidence-storage-failure/v1'; status = 'failed'; rawEvidenceFiles = $files.Count; rawEvidenceBytes = $rawBytes; rawLimitBytes = 35 * 1024 * 1024; archiveLimitBytes = 15 * 1024 * 1024; fullEvidenceUploaded = $false; derivedMetadataUploaded = $false; reason = 'The publication evidence exceeded its bounded artifact budget; only incomplete diagnostics are retained.' } | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $fallback 'storage-failure.json') -Encoding utf8\n+            $archive = Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-publication-incomplete-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ID + '-' + $env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT + '.zip')\n+            [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($fallback, $archive, [System.IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal, $false)\n+          }\n+          'artifact_path=' + $archive | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+          'complete=' + $complete.ToString().ToLowerInvariant() | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+          if (-not $complete) { throw 'Complete publication evidence exceeded the artifact budget; the uploaded fallback is incomplete.' }\n+\n+      - name: Preserve success or failure evidence\n+        if: always() && steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path != ''\n+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n+        with:\n+          name: publication-integrity-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}\n+          path: ${{ steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path }}\n+          if-no-files-found: error\n+          compression-level: 0\n+          retention-days: 1\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/windows-path-cloud.yml b/.github/workflows/windows-path-cloud.yml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..b830196\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.github/workflows/windows-path-cloud.yml\n@@ -0,0 +1,111 @@\n+name: Cloud Windows path experiment\n+\n+on:\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+  push:\n+    branches: [main]\n+    paths:\n+      - '.github/workflows/windows-path-cloud.yml'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/experiments/windows-path/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-windows-path-cloud.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/sync/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/editor/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/lib/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/server.mjs'\n+  pull_request:\n+    paths:\n+      - '.github/workflows/windows-path-cloud.yml'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/experiments/windows-path/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-windows-path-cloud.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud.mjs'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/sync/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/apps/editor/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/lib/**'\n+      - 'products/rea-studio/server.mjs'\n+\n+permissions:\n+  contents: read\n+concurrency:\n+  group: windows-path-experiment-${{ github.ref }}\n+  cancel-in-progress: false\n+\n+jobs:\n+  finite-windows-path:\n+    runs-on: windows-2022\n+    timeout-minutes: 15\n+    env:\n+      CI: 'true'\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Enable long research snapshot paths\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: git config --global core.longpaths true\n+      - name: Check out the exact committed baseline and inert source bundle\n+        id: checkout\n+        uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4\n+        with:\n+          persist-credentials: false\n+          fetch-depth: 1\n+      - name: Select pinned Node runtime\n+        uses: actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020 # v4\n+        with:\n+          node-version: '24.16.0'\n+          architecture: x64\n+          check-latest: false\n+      - name: Select owned evidence outside the source tree\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-windows-path-evidence-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          'REA_WINDOWS_PATH_EVIDENCE='+$evidence|Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_ENV -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+      - name: Compose exactly the three reviewed experimental source targets\n+        id: compose\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-windows-path-cloud.mjs --phase compose --evidence \"$env:REA_WINDOWS_PATH_EVIDENCE\"\n+      - name: Execute the fixed five-file Editor and Sync regression scope\n+        id: tests\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $composition=Join-Path $env:REA_WINDOWS_PATH_EVIDENCE 'windows-path-composition.json'\n+          node products/rea-studio/scripts/verify-cloud.mjs --scope windows-path-experiment --output \"$env:REA_WINDOWS_PATH_EVIDENCE\" --overlay-manifest \"$composition\" --timeout-ms 600000\n+      - name: Independently recheck the three composed sources after every observable attempt\n+        id: postcheck\n+        if: always() && steps.compose.outcome != '' && steps.compose.outcome != 'skipped'\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: node products/rea-studio/scripts/compose-windows-path-cloud.mjs --phase verify-after --evidence \"$env:REA_WINDOWS_PATH_EVIDENCE\"\n+      - name: Package bounded portable evidence after failures too\n+        id: evidence\n+        if: always()\n+        shell: pwsh\n+        run: |\n+          $evidence=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-windows-path-evidence-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+          New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $evidence -Force|Out-Null\n+          @{schema='rea-cloud-windows-path-workflow-attempt/v1';sourceCommit=$env:GITHUB_SHA;runId=$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID;runAttempt=$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT;runnerEnvironment=$env:RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT;checkoutOutcome='${{ steps.checkout.outcome }}';compositionOutcome='${{ steps.compose.outcome }}';testOutcome='${{ steps.tests.outcome }}';postcheckOutcome='${{ steps.postcheck.outcome }}';statusBeforePackaging='${{ job.status }}';productionInstalled=$false;historicalReceiptsRebound=$false;acceptancePreclaimed=$false}|ConvertTo-Json|Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $evidence 'windows-path-workflow-attempt.json') -Encoding utf8\n+          $archive=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-windows-path-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT+'.zip')\n+          Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem\n+          [IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($evidence,$archive,[IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal,$false)\n+          $limit=15*1024*1024;$bytes=(Get-Item -LiteralPath $archive).Length\n+          if($bytes -gt $limit){\n+            $fallback=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-windows-path-incomplete-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT)\n+            New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $fallback|Out-Null\n+            $retained=@();$omitted=@()\n+            foreach($file in Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $evidence -File){\n+              if($file.Length -le 1024*1024){Copy-Item -LiteralPath $file.FullName -Destination (Join-Path $fallback $file.Name);$retained+=$file.Name}\n+              elseif($file.Extension -eq '.txt'){$target=Join-Path $fallback ($file.BaseName+'.tail.txt');$logInput=[IO.File]::OpenRead($file.FullName);$logOutput=[IO.File]::Create($target);try{$logInput.Position=[Math]::Max(0,$logInput.Length-256*1024);$logInput.CopyTo($logOutput)}finally{$logOutput.Dispose();$logInput.Dispose()};$omitted+=@{file=$file.Name;originalBytes=$file.Length;tailOnly=$true}}\n+              else{$omitted+=@{file=$file.Name;bytes=$file.Length;tailOnly=$false}}\n+            }\n+            @{schema='rea-cloud-evidence-storage-failure/v1';status='failed';fullArchiveBytes=$bytes;limitBytes=$limit;completeEvidenceUploaded=$false;sourceSnapshotsUploaded=$false;retainedFiles=$retained;omittedOrTailed=$omitted;reason='Full Windows path evidence exceeded15MiB. This fallback is incomplete; source/raw backup acceptance is not established.'}|ConvertTo-Json -Depth 6|Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $fallback 'storage-failure.json') -Encoding utf8\n+            $archive=Join-Path $env:RUNNER_TEMP ('rea-windows-path-incomplete-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID+'-'+$env:GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT+'.zip')\n+            [IO.Compression.ZipFile]::CreateFromDirectory($fallback,$archive,[IO.Compression.CompressionLevel]::Optimal,$false)\n+            if((Get-Item -LiteralPath $archive).Length -le $limit){'artifact_path='+$archive|Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append}\n+            throw 'Full Windows path evidence exceeded15MiB; only an explicitly incomplete diagnostic fallback can be uploaded.'\n+          }\n+          'artifact_path='+$archive|Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_OUTPUT -Encoding utf8 -Append\n+      - name: Preserve the portable evidence archive\n+        if: always() && steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path != ''\n+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4\n+        with:\n+          name: windows-path-experiment-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}\n+          path: ${{ steps.evidence.outputs.artifact_path }}\n+          if-no-files-found: error\n+          compression-level: 0\n+          retention-days: 1\ndiff --git a/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md b/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f955403\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@\n+# Hosted verification and experimental Archive overlay\n+\n+The [later Flow/Vault and collector-control run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-controls-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **282/282 finite contract checks with zero skips** on revision `a2e0aa7`, using a standard GitHub-hosted `windows-2022` runner and Node `24.16.0`. Its 764-file census stayed exact during execution; all 342 active source snapshots, raw logs and synthetic control evidence have verified readable local backups. Four synthetic collector controls pass separately. The [initial finite run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) retains its earlier 282/762/340 epoch on `14e4859`; the historical 937/737 development checkpoint retains its own sources and receipt. Later runner/census changes need their own actual result. A new full ten-application suite, fresh browser acceptance and comparative acceptance remain pending.\n+\n+After opening the recovery pull request, the workflow runs for relevant pushes to `main`, pull requests, and manual dispatch, avoiding both a branch-push run and a pull-request run for the same update. Its three external actions are pinned to complete Git commit IDs. It requests only repository-content read access, retains no checkout credential, creates no cache or paid resource, and has a 30-minute job deadline. GitHub supplies `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true`; the bootstrap also requires `CI=true`, `RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT=github-hosted`, Windows and the exact Node version before doing any acquisition. It refuses normal local execution.\n+\n+## Original verification inputs\n+\n+`products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-flow-vault.mjs` acquires verification inputs on the hosted runner:\n+\n+- Flow: the committed oracle package and lock files populate ignored `.local/flow-original`. The lock SHA256 is authenticated, the selected Node-RED packages are pinned to `5.0.8` and the test helper to `0.3.6`, and the runner's npm installs with `ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund`. The existing tests independently authenticate selected original source bytes.\n+- Vault: the recorded KeePass `2.61.1` portable ZIP is fetched from the JiriSko GitHub mirror. The exact archive size and publisher-matching SHA256 recorded in `projects/07-keepass/artifact-manifest.json` are required before extraction. The complete portable package stays under ignored `.local/keepass-original`; the extracted `KeePass.exe` size and SHA256 are required before its path is exported to the suite. The transport is a third-party mirror. OpenPGP verification and reproducible-build verification are not claimed.\n+\n+Original packages and executable files are never included in the public source or evidence artifact. The application does not import the bootstrap or downloaded verification programs. The workflow does not start an original product service.\n+\n+`windows-tar-readiness.json` separately records the runner's `System32/tar.exe` SHA256 against the exact historical bsdtar oracle pin. A mismatch leaves the full development suite's Archive prerequisites unresolved; it does not fail this finite Flow/Vault acquisition. The readiness check reads bytes without executing tar. Portable ZIP extraction separately uses runner-provided tar, and the resulting original executable is authenticated.\n+\n+## Receipts and recoverable evidence\n+\n+Each GitHub run attempt gets a separate evidence directory under `RUNNER_TEMP`, outside the Studio source census. The bootstrap writes `prerequisite-acquisition.json` with running and terminal acquisition state. The test runner writes its own attempt receipt, streaming raw stdout/stderr, source inventories and snapshots, and events. Its exact selected tests and source-stability results, when completed, determine the scope of the result. Acquisition success alone is not a test pass.\n+\n+The Flow/Vault workflow includes four synthetic collector controls through `verify-cloud-controls.mjs`: an assertion failure after an early output marker, a deliberate skipped test, an owned source-file change, and a hanging test stopped by a one-second deadline. Each uses an isolated synthetic Git repository and visibly fake prerequisite receipt under `RUNNER_TEMP`. All four controls pass in run `38805892204` on `a2e0aa7`, preserving each intended failed attempt, early raw output and terminal evidence. They execute synthetic tests only; their counts stay separate from the 282 product checks. Run `38803745286` predates this addition and establishes no collector-control result. Acceptance of later collector changes requires a separate result.\n+\n+The later public capsule preserves every non-source-tree evidence file, including raw logs and all four controls' receipts, events and source manifests. It omits **402 source-snapshot payloads: 342 application snapshots and 60 synthetic snapshots**. Their exact identities remain in the preserved source inventories/manifests and omission list. The complete ZIP and all 463 readable files, including those omitted payloads, remain verified in the local backup. This capsule does not claim complete public source capture.\n+\n+The workflow always attempts to package available evidence as a portable ZIP and upload it with one-day retention. The complete compressed ZIP is capped at **15 MiB**. A larger ZIP fails the storage gate and uploads only a clearly marked, bounded diagnostic fallback; that fallback is not a complete evidence backup. No dependency or original-program cache is uploaded.\n+\n+Download the actual artifact contents promptly into the established authorized local work destination. Retain the portable evidence ZIP and readable extracted files; record the GitHub run URL, source commit, run ID and attempt. Verify the terminal receipt, raw-log readability, listed source identities and the copied prerequisite receipt. Keep acquisition, tests, browser checks and the full development checkpoint as distinct results. A URL, expiring GitHub artifact or placeholder alone does not establish a recoverable local backup. Failed, cancelled and incomplete attempts remain separate historical evidence; never complete an older attempt by substituting a rerun's files.\n+\n+Artifact storage is shared with the account's other repositories and runs. The one-job, one-day, 15 MiB configuration bounds this workflow's requested storage; it does not assert available account quota. GitHub-hosted public-repository execution is the intended supported environment. Do not change billing, select a paid runner or increase the artifact budget without authorization.\n+\n+## Separate Archive experiment\n+\n+[The Archive workflow](.github/workflows/archive-aes-cloud.yml) prepares a separate hosted experiment from the inert `products/rea-studio/experiments/archive-aes` bundle. [The first attempt38805892328](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-aes-composition-failed-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) failed baseline source-census qualification on `a2e0aa7`, before any overlay transition, original acquisition or test execution. Its two artifact files, local backup attestation and job log remain preserved as that failed epoch.\n+\n+[The earlier attempt38806502120](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-metadata-failure-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) composed the overlay on baseline `9970992`, acquired the original verification inputs and executed the thirteen selected test files: **160 checks, 154 passes, six failures and zero skips**. Its 776-file census remained stable during execution; the separate post-run source check also passed. Six failures concern DOS short-path versus long-path aliases in hosted Windows source metadata. This attempt remains a separate failed epoch.\n+\n+This failure capsule retains all 18 non-source artifact files, including raw output, composition/acquisition receipts and both observation files, plus the job log and local backup attestation. Its **354 omitted `verification/source/` snapshot payloads** remain in the complete, byte-verified 372-file readable local backup. Their identities and source manifests remain public. Source stability and the failed test outcome are separate recorded facts; the full Archive and ten-application suites remain open.\n+\n+[The earlier attempt38808025295](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-prerequisites-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) ran on the composed overlay based on `b15d166`: **161 checks, 155 passes, six failures and zero skips**, with a stable 779-file census. Its path-spelling diagnostic records `differentSpelling=true` for the hosted short-name temporary path and its long-name form. This failed epoch remains preserved separately from the later literal-path correction.\n+\n+That capsule preserves all 32 non-source artifact files, including every prerequisite receipt and acquisition log, the candidate raw output and both observations, plus the job log and backup attestation. Its **357 omitted source-snapshot payloads** remain in the complete, verified 389-file local backup. Their identities and manifests remain public. Its prerequisite phases passed separately from its failed candidate result.\n+\n+[The later attempt38808918976](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-aes-finite-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **161/161 finite experimental checks**, with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos, after the literal-path correction. Its actual tested Git baseline is merge `7d5bde3fb94e3383e6d85e50e7d567516cc6202c` at `refs/pull/1/merge`; PR head `aeb62e6` is a separate identity. The composition manifest SHA256 is `4fe7b114341199fa31d5553ffb3505db0e3427337ea8c72c637a8d5a3501a042`. The 779-file composed census remained stable, and the separate post-run source check passed. All three ZIP, plain-7Z and encrypted-7Z path diagnostics retain `differentSpelling=true`, showing `RUNNER~1` paths resolving to `runneradmin` paths while the physical timestamp checks pass.\n+\n+The successful finite capsule preserves all **32 non-source artifact files**, including metadata, prerequisite receipts and logs, raw test output and both observations, plus the job log, local backup attestation and preservation collector. Its **357 source-snapshot payloads** are explicitly omitted publicly and remain in the complete, byte-verified **389-file** readable local backup. Their exact paths, sizes and digests remain in the public omission list and source manifests. Finite experimental contracts pass; production installation remains false, and browser acceptance, the full Archive scope and the full ten-application suite remain pending.\n+\n+`compose-archive-aes-cloud.mjs` authenticates the committed baseline and selected experimental source bytes, then composes an explicit overlay in the ephemeral hosted checkout. The changes include selected AES/container behavior and source timestamp collection. `composition.json` records the baseline Git commit, approved source identities and the composed source census; the test collector receives it through `--overlay-manifest`. Each tested source identity combines its actual baseline commit and composition manifest. A stable before/after census describes that attempt's composed bytes and does not equate them with the Git baseline. The composition is confined to the experimental hosted checkout; production installation remains false.\n+\n+Original 7-Zip acquisition, overlay composition, execution and post-run checks produce separate evidence. Future experimental results must retain their actual run ID, raw logs, exact sources and local backups. Their counts remain separate from the finite 282 Flow/Vault checks, the four synthetic collector controls and the historical 937 development checks. The experiment leaves the full ten-application suite and comparative acceptance pending.\n+\n+## Remaining broader verification work\n+\n+In the successful finite run38808918976, `bootstrap-cloud-bsdtar.mjs` acquired the exact Microsoft `tar.exe` and adjacent `archiveint.dll` pair from official image endpoints. `verify-cloud-bsdtar.mjs` separately recorded **one successful original `--version` process**, with zero candidate comparisons. These prerequisite phases also passed in earlier run38808025295. The EXE retains the historical digest; the paired DLL has a newly explicit identity. Loaded module paths were not independently observed, and this result does not establish which DLL the earlier EXE-only historical run loaded. The reviewed paired-image test-loader overlay still needs its own broader replay.\n+\n+`bootstrap-cloud-development.mjs` also completed acquisition in that run: **four Automation archives and 4,350 authenticated source files, 202 routing-cache files, three Sketch assets, and two Restic assets (archive and executable)**, with zero skipped prerequisites. Its bounded acquisition logs and receipt are preserved. Automation's acquisition command initializes released original modules for integrity checking; that disclosed initialization is separate from comparative tests. This bootstrap ran zero comparative test processes and started zero original application services.\n+\n+Linux coverage is deferred. An identical Linux certificate would be misleading because current original-product comparisons use Windows PowerShell and Windows executables. The existing full development verifier additionally requires every prerequisite and zero skipped tests; this workflow's finite receipt cannot replace it.\n+\n+A full-suite replay still requires its own clean hosted checkout, repeated prerequisite authentication, the reviewed paired-image test-loader composition and a complete zero-skip test result. Acquired inputs and one version smoke do not establish that acceptance. Fresh browser checks and independent checkpoint acceptance also remain separate work. All earlier receipts preserve their original source attribution.\n+\n+The [full current-suite attempt 38810678336](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-full-suite-failed-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) is a completed failure: 1,042 tests, 1,024 passes, 18 failures and no skips/cancellations/todos. It tested actual merge `abcac0b2f7905838198bdaa2e11461ac52cdb75e`, separately from PR head `6f89a09`, with exactly three reviewed oracle-loader test sources composed and zero application-runtime changes. All prerequisites and the separate source postcheck passed; 770 eligible sources stayed stable. The public capsule retains 60 logical records/41 objects, including all non-source artifact files and raw wrapper output. Its 348 omitted active source payloads remain in the complete verified readable local backup. One Editor assertion observes canonical versus short root spelling; 17 Sync WebDAV cases stop at the alias guard. Both areas require source-reviewed corrections and new hosted execution. Passing 1,024 checks does not turn this failed run into acceptance.\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 41ff4c2..e8c6d5f 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -51,4 +51,18 @@ The historical [search, Save, notebook trash and entry recycling checkpoint](pro\n \n The historical [notebook confirmation, drawing layout and editor value API checkpoint](products/rea-studio/NOTES-LAYOUT-VALUE-API-MILESTONE.md) passes **847 implemented-contract checks,0skips and720stable source fingerprints**. Notes passes69focused checks and8browser groups; Sketch39app/2HTTP checks and14browser groups; Editor API13pure checks. Source snapshots, confirmed failures, strictness/precision corrections, independent review and exact historical host transitions remain inspectable. Zero products satisfy the accepted complete replacement and comparative standard.\n \n-The current [Editor pattern search and Vault group recovery checkpoint](products/rea-studio/EDITOR-PATTERN-VAULT-GROUP-MILESTONE.md) passes **937 implemented-contract checks, no skips and 737 stable source fingerprints**. It adds bounded pattern search, corrected native textarea navigation and recursive Vault group recovery. Exact sources, independent negative reviews, original comparisons and finite browser limits are preserved. Full replacements and comparative acceptance remain under development.\n+The last published [Editor pattern search and Vault group recovery checkpoint](products/rea-studio/EDITOR-PATTERN-VAULT-GROUP-MILESTONE.md) passes **937 implemented-contract checks, no skips and 737