ts 779-file census stayed stable and 357 source snapshots are backed up locally. Acquisition of the pinned bsdtar EXE/DLL pair and other development inputs succeeded, and one separate original `--version` smoke passed. This failed source epoch remains preserved.\n+\n+The [later Archive finite experiment](results/cloud-archive-aes-finite-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **161/161 checks with zero failures or skips** after the literal-path correction. Run `38808918976` tested the composed overlay on actual Git merge `7d5bde3`, distinct from PR head `aeb62e6`; its 779-file census remained stable. The path diagnostics confirm real short-name/long-name aliases while the metadata checks pass. All 389 evidence files, including 357 source snapshots, remain in the verified local backup; the public capsule retains all non-source evidence and the omitted snapshots' identities. Original prerequisites, the separate one-process bsdtar smoke and the post-run source check also passed. Production installation remains false; browser acceptance, the full Archive scope and the full ten-application suite remain pending.\n+\n+The [full hosted replay](results/cloud-full-suite-failed-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) now records 1,042 checks: 1,024 passed, 18 failed and zero skipped, with 770 stable source identities and 348 backed-up active snapshots. It used actual merge `abcac0b2` and the explicit three-source paired-oracle test overlay. The failures concern the Editor Git root observer and Sync WebDAV short Windows root paths. Corrections and a focused hosted replay are pending; the failed record does not replace historical receipts or establish current full-suite acceptance.\ndiff --git a/products/rea-studio/STATUS.json b/products/rea-studio/STATUS.json\nindex 3c75a58..6b9619c 100644\n--- a/products/rea-studio/STATUS.json\n+++ b/products/rea-studio/STATUS.json\n@@ -1,213 +1,439 @@\n-{\n-  \"schema\": \"rea-product-development-status/v1\",\n-  \"accepted_scope\": \"Every documented feature of the original products; speed, resource use, ease of use, compatibility and reliability\",\n-  \"phase\": \"editor-pattern-vault-group-recovery\",\n-  \"completion_status\": \"incomplete\",\n-  \"complete_replacement_products\": 0,\n-  \"initial_applications\": 10,\n-  \"whole_product_release_crosswalk\": \"initial records available; some complete-product/platform/edition bindings remain unresolved\",\n-  \"requirements_crosswalk\": \"requirements/README.md\",\n-  \"exhaustive_frozen_feature_inventory\": \"not complete; documentation-file catalogs are not exhaustive feature extraction\",\n-  \"full_feature_parity\": \"not-established\",\n-  \"full_product_performance_comparison\": \"not-established\",\n-  \"comparative_usability_study\": \"not-performed\",\n-  \"full_vendor_format_and_protocol_compatibility\": \"not-established\",\n-  \"long_run_and_fault_injection_reliability\": \"not-established\",\n-  \"universal_superiority\": \"not-established\",\n-  \"external_security_assessment\": \"not-performed\",\n-  \"no_completion_notification_should_be_sent\": true,\n-  \"next_required_milestone\": \"Continue every documented original feature and all requested quality dimensions. Correct the independently reproduced next-stage Vault group-editor draft loss; accept native Flow links; continue multiline/replace/encoding/extension lifecycle, dashboards/calculations, provider/plugin behavior, drawing bindings/fonts/rotation, synchronization, native formats and reliability. Complete release-bound atomic inventories and comparative speed, resource and usability acceptance.\",\n-  \"implemented_milestone\": \"Whole-word and selected JavaScript regular-expression workspace search with bounded workers and corrected native textarea navigation; recursive Vault group preview, recycle, purge and previous-parent restoration. 937 implemented-contract checks pass with no skips and 737 stable source files.\",\n-  \"current_milestone_record\": \"EDITOR-PATTERN-VAULT-GROUP-MILESTONE.md\",\n-  \"current_browser_record\": \"apps/notes/results/inline-confirmation-followup/corrected-browser/validation.json.snapshot\",\n-  \"goal_status\": \"active\",\n-  \"other_browser_records\": [\n-    {\n-      \"path\": \"apps/sketch/results/layout-followup/browser/frozen/validation.json.snapshot\",\n-      \"role\": \"14finite actual Chrome workflows on the corrected188-file candidate and a10-source private host; recorded private one-line host adapter distinct from later production staticMap insertion; download file delivery unverified.\"\n-    },\n-    {\n-      \"path\": \"results/editor-workspace-search-followup/prior-browser/frozen/validation.json.snapshot\",\n-      \"role\": \"Seven actual search workflows on earlier124 correction; source-stable and exact, but not current126 path or119 Save browser acceptance.\"\n-    },\n-    {\n-      \"path\": \"apps/vault/results/history-followup/final-independent-review/browser-proof/validation.json.snapshot\",\n-      \"role\": \"Accepted exact-source held Save/Restore browser study and host restart, retained in the independent-review stage; locate the exact source path in its preservation manifest.\"\n-    },\n-    {\n-      \"path\": \"results/milestones/rabin-routing-geometry-browser-20261012/snapshot-manifest.json\",\n-      \"role\": \"Frozen Backup/first-Automation/Sketch checkpoint before recovery/collector changes; source intervals explicitly recorded\"\n-    },\n-    {\n-      \"path\": \"results/browser-compression-remote-verification.json\",\n-      \"role\": \"Historical b9f6b71 compression/remote checkpoint\"\n-    },\n-    {\n-      \"path\": \"results/browser-automation-recovery-20261012/validation.json\",\n-      \"role\": \"Current unchanged Automation source browser check\"\n-    }\n-  ],\n-  \"current_focus_checks\": {\n-    \"backup_pack_integration\": 64,\n-    \"notes_notebook_trash_integration\": 69,\n-    \"automation_recovery_routing_original_editor\": 74,\n-    \"ske